# DESCRIPTION
# Fraction story problem.
# ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Arithmetic')
## DBchapter('Fractions')
## DBsection('Word problems')
## KEYWORDS('word problem','fraction','m&ms')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')
## Date('04/05/2021')

#updated 2023.03.17

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'contextFraction.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Fraction");

do { $denom = random(3, 6); $x = random(1, $denom - 1); }
    until gcd($x, $denom) == 1;
$y      = $denom - $x;
$z      = random(4, 6);
$num1   = Real($x * $z);
$num2   = Real($y * $z);
$diff   = abs($num1 - $num2);
$total  = $num1 + $num2;
$fract1 = Compute("$x/$denom");
$fract2 = Compute("$y/$denom");

@colors = random_subset(2, 'orange', 'brown', 'red', 'green', 'blue', 'yellow');

BEGIN_PGML

There is a bag of M&M's that are only [$colors[0]] and [$colors[1]]. [`[$fract1]`] of the
bag are [$colors[0]].

a) What fraction of the bag of M&M's are [$colors[1]]? [_____]{$fract2}

b) If there are [`[$num2]`] M&M's that are [$colors[1]], how many M&M's are there
alltogether? [________]{$total}

c) How many more [@ $x>$y ? $colors[0] : $colors[1] @] M&M's are there than 
[@ $x < $y ? $colors[0] : $colors[1] @] ones?  [________]{$diff}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION

a) The fraction of orange M&M's is [`1-[$fract_brown]=[$fract_orange]`]

b) We know that [`[$fract_orange]`] units is [`[$num_orange]`], so [`\frac{1}{5}`] is [`[$z]`].
 If [`\frac{1}{5}`] of a unit is [`[$z]`], then one unit is [`[$total]`].  There
are a total of [`[$total]`] M&M's.

c) If there are [`[$total]`] M&M's altogether
and there are [`[$num_orange]`] orange M&M's, there are [`[$total]-[$num_orange]=[$num_brown]`]
more brown than orange M&M's.

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
